Task 3.3 – Translate the Recurrence into Pseudocode (4 Marks)
Algorithm: ZeroOneKnapsack

Objective: Find the maximum total value and identify the actual items selected without exceeding the vehicle capacity.

Pseudocode

text
ALGORITHM ZeroOneKnapsack

BEGIN

    READ N
    READ Capacity

    FOR i ← 1 TO N DO
        READ ItemID[i]
        READ Weight[i]
        READ Value[i]
    END FOR

    FOR w ← 0 TO Capacity DO
        DP[0][w] ← 0
    END FOR

    FOR i ← 0 TO N DO
        DP[i][0] ← 0
    END FOR

    FOR i ← 1 TO N DO

        FOR w ← 1 TO Capacity DO

            IF Weight[i] > w THEN

                DP[i][w] ← DP[i-1][w]

            ELSE

                IncludeValue ← Value[i] +
                               DP[i-1][w-Weight[i]]

                ExcludeValue ← DP[i-1][w]

                DP[i][w] ← MAX(IncludeValue,
                               ExcludeValue)

            END IF

        END FOR

    END FOR

    MaximumValue ← DP[N][Capacity]

    RemainingCapacity ← Capacity

    FOR i ← N DOWNTO 1 DO

        IF DP[i][RemainingCapacity] ≠
           DP[i-1][RemainingCapacity] THEN

            Selected[i] ← TRUE

            RemainingCapacity ←
                RemainingCapacity - Weight[i]

        ELSE

            Selected[i] ← FALSE

        END IF

    END FOR

    WRITE "Selected Items"

    FOR i ← 1 TO N DO

        IF Selected[i] = TRUE THEN
            WRITE ItemID[i]
        END IF

    END FOR

    WRITE "Maximum Total Value:", MaximumValue

    WRITE "Total Weight:", Capacity - RemainingCapacity

    RETURN Selected, MaximumValue

END ALGORITHM
Explanation of the Pseudocode
Input: Read the number of items, capacity, item IDs, weights and values.

Initialisation: Set all states involving zero items or zero capacity to zero.

State computation: Process items one by one and capacities from 1 to the maximum capacity.

Include/exclude decision: Compare the value obtained by including the current item with the value obtained by excluding it.

Optimal value: Store the maximum achievable value in each DP state.

Reconstruction: Start from DP[N][Capacity] and move backwards through the DP table to identify selected items.

Output: Display the selected item IDs, maximum total value and total weight.

Important: During reconstruction, the algorithm subtracts the weight of a selected item from the remaining capacity. This ensures that the selected items are identified correctly and no item is selected more than once.

